{
  "text": " Okay, I found the oversized travel bag that's actually chic. This is the Eleanor Weekender from Velantra. It's a Birkin-inspired shape scaled up to travel size. Full-grain leather over woven canvas, solid brass hardware, and no logo anywhere on it. It's 18 inches wide, so it holds three days of clothes, my laptop and my chargers, and it still keeps its shape packed full. The inside is caramel leather with a slip pocket, and the flap folds all the way back so you can see everything. I've carried it on every trip since June. It sits on top of my carry-on, it slides straight into the overhead bin, and I haven't checked a bag once. I get asked if it's designer constantly. It comes in four colors, and if you want the classic black, that one's a pre-order and ships mid-September. They're running a sale right now, and the colors always sell out. I left the link below.",
